            "creator": "jaganmn2",
            "bug_id": 18779,
            "text": "```\n> m <- function(...) { cat(\"a\\n\"); NextMethod() }\n> for (generic in c(\"c\", \"cbind\", \"rbind\")) .S3method(generic, \"a\", m)\n> x <- structure(0, class = \"a\")\n> c(x)\na\n[1] 0\n> cbind(x)\na\nError in NextMethod() : generic function not specified\n> rbind(x)\na\nError in NextMethod() : generic function not specified\n```\n\nThe error message suggests that the method call is not evaluated in an environment containing the variables `.Generic`, `.Method`, `.Class`, etc. essential for correct `NextMethod()` dispatch.  Indeed:\n\n```\n> debug(m)\n> c(x)\ndebugging in: c.a(x)\ndebug at #1: {\n    cat(\"a\\n\")\n    NextMethod()\n}\nBrowse[1]> ls(all.names = TRUE)\n[1] \"...\"             \".Class\"          \".Generic\"        \".GenericCallEnv\"\n[5] \".GenericDefEnv\"  \".Group\"          \".Method\"        \nBrowse[1]> Q\n> cbind(x)\ndebugging in: cbind(deparse.level, ...)\ndebug at #1: {\n    cat(\"a\\n\")\n    NextMethod()\n}\nBrowse[1]> ls(all.names = TRUE)\n[1] \"...\"\nBrowse[1]> Q\n> rbind(x)\ndebugging in: rbind(deparse.level, ...)\ndebug at #1: {\n    cat(\"a\\n\")\n    NextMethod()\n}\nBrowse[1]> ls(all.names = TRUE)\n[1] \"...\"\nBrowse[1]> Q\n```\n\nComparing `do_c` and `do_bind`, both defined in `bind.c`, it seems clear that the difference is that `do_c` calls `DispatchAnyOrEval` whereas `do_bind` performs method look-up and evaluation \"manually\", notably _not_ constructing a special environment for evaluation of the method call.\n\nIt is well documented (e.g., in `help(\"cbind\")` and by comments in the body of of `do_bind`) that internal generic functions dispatching on `...` are likely to behave specially.  Still, I wonder if we should aim to have `do_c` and `do_bind` share more code and ultimately use the same mechanism for dispatch.\n\nLuke made a similar comment in bug 18579, comment 4:\n\n> All that said, the differences in implementation between `do_c()` and `do_bind()` seem a little odd and it might be worth looking into sharing more code.",
            "count": 0,
            "is_markdown": true,
            "tags": [],
            "attachment_id": {},
            "id": 101126,
            "time": "2024-08-13T16:30:59Z",
            "is_private": false
          },
          {
            "creation_time": "2026-09-01T14:14:49Z",
            "creator": "AHL27",
            "is_markdown": true,
            "count": 1,
            "bug_id": 18779,
            "text": "Created attachment 3811\nPotential do_bind.c dispatch fix\n\nRoot cause seems to be `do_bind.c:1127`:\n\n```\nSEXP ans = applyClosure(call, method, args, env, R_NilValue, TRUE);\n```\n\n`R_NilValue` is passed as the fifth argument (`suppliedvars`), meaning that we lose `.Generic`, `.Method`, `.Class`, etc.\n\nI put together a quick patch that does resolve the issue by just injecting the correct variables into `applyClosure` here.\n\nI'm not sure that this is overall the right way to go, because (as previously mentioned) it's probably better to unify this interface rather than continuing to implement hand-rolled parsing. That's a much larger change though, and I thought this would at least be a good starting point to continue the discussion.",
            "attachment_id": 3811,
            "tags": [],
            "is_private": false,
            "id": 103511,
            "time": "2026-09-01T14:14:49Z"
          },
          {
            "text": "Wanted to add a little more context on what's going on in this patch.\n\nThe tl;dr here is that we're populating a new `env` with the right args to be able to call method dispatch (`.Generic`, `.Method`, `.Class`, etc.). This is done via `createS3Vars`, and it allows `NextMethod` to correctly locate the next method.\n\nMost of the code added is actually just detecting when we're trying to execute the default `cbind.default` / `rbind.default` generic. \n\n`c/rbind.default` is implemented as `.Internal(c/rbind(...))`, which just calls into `do_bind`. This means that if we have no checks and the base class dispatches to `cbind.default`, we'll re-enter do_bind and loop forever:\n\n```\ncbind.my_class -> NextMethod -> cbind.default -> do_bind -> detects my_class\n     ^                                                             |\n      \\____________________________________________________________/\n\n```\n\nThe added checks ensure that if we're already at the \"end\" of the dispatch chain (i.e., at the default method), we just fall through to the default C-level `bind` logic later on in the function rather than continuing to try to dispatch further:\n\n```\ncbind.my_class -> NextMethod -> cbind.default -> detected default -> C-level bind\n```",
            "bug_id": 18779,
